From 8a944275fdc7dc978eb6f8a344eda76a8f390604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keerthana K <keerthana.kalyanasundaram@broadcom.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Mar 2026 04:57:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] abi/4.0: adjust for kernel 6.12 feature support

The abi/4.0 file shipped with apparmor 4.1.6 declares features that
do not match what the kernel 6.12 AppArmor module actually exposes.
Fix the two mismatches:

1. ipc/posix_mqueue: POSIX message queue mediation is not yet
   upstreamed into the mainline kernel. Remove the ipc section.

2. policy/permstable32_version: The kernel 6.12 only supports
   permstable32 version 1 (0x000001), not version 2. Downgrade
   to match.

Signed-off-by: Keerthana K <keerthana.kalyanasundaram@broadcom.com>
---
 profiles/apparmor.d/abi/4.0 | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/profiles/apparmor.d/abi/4.0 b/profiles/apparmor.d/abi/4.0
index 9e61fe3..9a1cfd9 100644
--- a/profiles/apparmor.d/abi/4.0
+++ b/profiles/apparmor.d/abi/4.0
@@ -31,9 +31,6 @@ version {1.2
 file {mask {create read write exec append mmap_exec link lock
 }
 }
-ipc {posix_mqueue {create read write open delete setattr getattr
-}
-}
 mount {mask {mount umount pivot_root
 }
 }
@@ -56,7 +53,7 @@ policy {outofband {0x000001
 }
 permstable32 {allow deny subtree cond kill complain prompt audit quiet hide xindex tag label
 }
-permstable32_version {0x000002
+permstable32_version {0x000001
 }
 set_load {yes
 }
-- 
2.43.7

